---
import Prose from "~/components/Prose.astro";
import PageLayout from "~/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { personSchema } from "~/utils/personSchema";
---

<PageLayout
  seo={{
    title: "About Nirjan Khadka | Senior Software Engineer — Backend & Full Stack",
    description:
      "I'm Nirjan, a senior software engineer with 7+ years building web products, backend services and operational tooling. Based in Nepal, open to sponsored relocation or eligible remote work.",
    canonical: "https://nirjan.dev/about",
    openGraph: {
      basic: {
        title:
          "About Nirjan Khadka | Backend & Full-Stack Engineer",
        type: "website",
        image: "https://nirjan.dev/images/site-og.png",
        url: "https://nirjan.dev/about",
      },
    },
  }}
  schemaGraphItems={[personSchema]}
>
  <div class="max-w-prose mx-auto py-6 px-3 lg:text-lg">
    <Prose>
      <h1>About me</h1>
      <img
        class="w-32 h-32 mb-1 mr-6 rounded-full float-left"
        src="/images/profile.webp"
        alt="Nirjan Khadka's profile picture"
      />
      <p>
        I'm Nirjan, a senior software engineer based in Nepal. I build backend
        services and full-stack products, and like following a feature from its
        data model and API through to the interface and production behaviour.
        I have 7+ years of software development experience. These days I work
        mainly with TypeScript, Node.js and Postgres, as well as production Go
        services and frontend work with Vue, Nuxt and React.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm based in Nepal and open to sponsored relocation or remote work
        where I'm legally eligible. You can reach me at
        <a href="mailto:hi@nirjan.dev">hi@nirjan.dev</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Work I've been doing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Clickout:</strong> fixed out-of-memory failures in queue-mode
          n8n workers, moved execution and binary storage to R2 with retention
          controls, and built tracing and operational dashboards. I moved
          permissions into a standalone API with roles, audit history and
          impersonation, and worked on production Go feed parsing and AI
          workflow guardrails, evaluations and fallback sourcing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Athlos (February–December 2025):</strong> worked on a B2B
          tournament SaaS, including a creation-flow MVP used by 92+ creators,
          billing for 6+ tenants, white-label themes and six-language support.
          I introduced Storybook and Playwright, and used PostHog and Grafana
          to understand product usage and WebSocket behaviour.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gfinity (December 2020–September 2024):</strong> migrated
          services, including Go services, from GCP to Fly.io, reducing hosting
          costs by 93%. I also built Node.js stock and price scraping that
          reduced scraping costs by 80%.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Selected projects</h2>
      <p>
        Outside work, I build tools I want to use myself. These personal
        projects show different parts of how I work; the public code is linked
        below.
      </p>
      <h3>
        <a href="https://github.com/nirjan-dev/remotedevjobs-v2">
          RemoteDevJobs
        </a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        A remote developer job board built with Nuxt 4, PostgreSQL and Drizzle.
        It brings several job feeds into a relational data model, with source
        adapters, a database-backed ingestion queue and filtered, server-rendered
        job listings.
        <a href="https://remotedevjobs.vercel.app">Visit the job board</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>
        <a href="https://github.com/nirjan-dev/safecap">SafeCap</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        A Chrome extension for recording a screen, window or tab, built with Vue
        and WXT. Recording chunks are streamed to the browser's Origin Private
        File System, with library metadata kept separately in Chrome storage.
        <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/safecap/jbghdaimglclkedejlobbpmfiealoepf">
          View it on the Chrome Web Store</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>
        <a href="https://github.com/nirjan-dev/litsi">Litsi</a>
      </h3>
      <p>
        A video-chat prototype with a Nuxt WebSocket signalling service and
        WebRTC audio and video. Room membership lives in server memory; calls
        can use a TURN relay when a direct peer connection is not possible.
        <a href="https://litsi.fly.dev">Try the prototype</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've also built
        <a href="https://github.com/nirjan-dev/rosetide">Rosetide</a>, a
        local-first period tracker with browser-local data and CSV backup.
      </p>


      <h2>How I like to work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Start with the user's problem. Keep interfaces clear, accessible and
          fast, and follow a feature through from the data model to the screen.
        </li>
        <li>
          Understand the fundamentals before adding abstractions. Prefer simple,
          well-understood tools and use profiling, debugging and tests to guide changes.
        </li>
        <li>
          Treat security, privacy, backups and observability as part of the
          product, not something to bolt on after shipping.
        </li>
        <li>
          Ship small changes, learn from feedback and iterate. Give teammates
          the benefit of the doubt and share what I learn.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I enjoy Linux, self-hosting and owning my data. I'm interested in how
        systems fit together, but I still care just as much about a useful
        interface and a good experience for the person using it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from coding, I'm a cinephile and enjoy books, history, mythology and
        storytelling. I listen to a lot of hip-hop, play football or futsal
        whenever I can, and support Manchester United.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
